    "Snippet": {
      "ChannelId": "UCiZeuI-7OPs7TmMel6Q5Msw",
      "ChannelTitle": "Kanishk Nishar",
      "Description": "This concerto was written and conducted by Stanis\u0142aw Skrowaczewski.  He was the long time director of the Minnesota Orchestra.  The soloist is Thomas Stacy.  This LP recording was originally issued on Desto Records in 1971.\n\nThe Orchestra performed this piece in Carnegie Hall in 1971.  The New York Times critic who heard the Concerto was less than enthused referring to it as \u0022not modern\u0022 and that in the end it was \u0022a mess.\u0022  At the same time, he found the performance of the orchestra to be excellent, and praised Skrowaczewski\u0027s conducting. Of Thomas Stacy, he said \u0022Stacy must be the Horowitz of the English Horn.\u0022\n\nHe also noted the rarity of a concerto for the English Horn - saying, \u0022it\u0027s as rare as finding fur on fish.\u0022\n\nI am posting as part of an effort to share works that are not on Youtube already and that are no longer in print.",
